(footprint "buck-module-universal"
  (version 20240108)
  (generator "luxdmx-carrier-gen_footprints")
  (layer "F.Cu")
  (descr "generic Universal 12-24V -> 5V regulator spot: MP1584-class corner-pad modules, Pololu D24V10F5 / D36V28F5, 3-pin 78xx-style SIP socket. Generated from modules.json, confidence=USER-SPECIFIED. Source: user spec 2026-08-01, shrunk 2026-08-13: modules in this class run from about 22 x 18 to 30 x 18 mm, so their pins sit about 18-26 mm apart across and 12-15 mm apart up the board. Pads are 12 x 5 mm on a 24 / 12 mm grid, which covers 12-36 mm across and 7-17 mm up. The first cut was 16 x 10 mm, generous in both directions; the height was insurance against a spread that does not exist, since every module in this class is 18 mm wide, and it cost 640 mm2 of solid back-side copper right where the signals cross to the right-hand headers. 240 mm2 now. Extended 2026-11-21: two 0.1 in rows and two M2 holes for fixed 5 V modules, in the gap between the right-hand lands. Pin positions from the vendors' own drawings: Pololu d24v10fx dimension PDF + drill guide reg17a01-drill.dxf (5 pins on 0.1 in, 0.05 in in from the short edge and the side), Pololu d36v28fx dimension PDF + reg24g-drill.dxf (edge row at x 0.25-0.65 in, y 0.05 in; PG at 0.25/0.15 in; holes 2.18 mm at 0.085 in from two opposite corners), RECOM R-78E-1.0 datasheet p.4 and Mornsun K78xx-1000R3(L) datasheet p.4 (pin 1 +Vin, 2 GND, 3 +Vout, 2.54 mm).")
